Bluesky — @bsky.app/expo-scroll-edge-effect
https://github.com/bluesky-social/expo-scroll-edge-effect

`ios/ScrollEdgeEffectView.swift` began as a port of `ExpoScrollEdgeEffectView.swift`
and has since been substantially rewritten: the Expo Modules API was dropped in
favour of resolving the target scroll view through the React Native bridge, and
the ownership registry, edge-effect style save/restore, trait observation,
shape element and Xcode compatibility guards are not derived from that project.

That project declares the MIT License in its `package.json`. It ships no LICENSE
file, so there is no upstream copyright notice to reproduce here.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

@callstack/liquid-glass
https://github.com/callstackincubator/liquid-glass

The iOS 26 support check in `ios/ScrollEdgeEffectModule.mm` is derived from
`LiquidGlassModule.mm`, with the class probe changed from `UIGlassEffect` to
`UIScrollEdgeElementContainerInteraction`.

